From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: no "Google API keys are missing" bar

Chromium builds without Google's API keys show an infobar in every new
browser window: "Google API keys are missing. Some functionality of
Chromium will be disabled." NickelOS is built without them (local
accounts, no Google sign-in or sync), so the bar only alarms people about
how the OS is made. It is not shown on ChromeOS builds.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/startup/infobar_utils.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/startup/infobar_utils.cc
index 598e361a29886..f2c123082f6fc 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/startup/infobar_utils.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/startup/infobar_utils.cc
@@ -253,6 +253,9 @@ void AddInfoBarsIfNecessary(BrowserWindowInterface* browser,
   infobars::ContentInfoBarManager* infobar_manager =
       infobars::ContentInfoBarManager::FromWebContents(web_contents);
 
+  // NickelOS: no Google API keys, by design (Google's services want its keys
+  // and accounts); the bar about them only alarmed users.
+#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
   if (!google_apis::HasAPIKeyConfigured()) {
     if (infobars::IsInfoBarMigrated(
             infobars::InfoBarDelegate::GOOGLE_API_KEYS_INFOBAR_DELEGATE)) {
@@ -266,6 +269,7 @@ void AddInfoBarsIfNecessary(BrowserWindowInterface* browser,
       GoogleApiKeysInfoBarDelegate::Create(infobar_manager);
     }
   }
+#endif
 
   if (ObsoleteSystem::IsObsoleteNowOrSoon()) {
     PrefService* local_state = g_browser_process->local_state();
